        "ended_at": "2026-06-15T16:52:53.000Z",
        "title": "Analytics rebuilt around a typed registry and contract CI gate",
        "summary": "Aura's metrics pipeline was reworked end to end so True DAU, retention, and reliability numbers stop silently drifting when code changes.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Client analytics now flow through a typed event registry with AST and pipeline tests that fail the build if an event is renamed, dropped, or passed as a non-literal, and if the client ever stops forwarding events to the Mixpanel SDK.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "57b077e8e3596117c08ce0ae032de9bd8e60386c"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "session_active is now emitted server-side from a single emitter, with Rust tests enforcing the event-name and manifest invariants so True DAU can't be double-counted or quietly lost.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "57b077e8e3596117c08ce0ae032de9bd8e60386c"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "A new Analytics Contract workflow runs the client and server analytics tests on every PR and direct push to main, gating merges the moment tracking would break.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "57b077e8e3596117c08ce0ae032de9bd8e60386c"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "iOS, Android, and desktop release lanes now bake VITE_MIXPANEL_TOKEN into the shipped bundle and hard-fail the build under REQUIRE_ANALYTICS, fixing the case where store-shipped clients silently no-op'd analytics; mobile chat input also picks up missing tracking.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "57b077e8e3596117c08ce0ae032de9bd8e60386c"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      }
